This repository adapts recipe material from other Apache-2.0 projects. Each adapted file names its source in its header and keeps the source's notices; the changes are described there.

- MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104 (https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104), Copyright 2026 Mia's AI Lab, Apache-2.0. recipes/glm53-mia/Dockerfile and recipes/glm53-kelchm/Dockerfile are adapted from its docker/Dockerfile. None of the kit's engine patches is copied here; they reach the engine fork, kelchm/TensorFold, as commits. glm53-mia imports the whole kit onto deploy/glm53-mia. glm53-kelchm adapts some of its patches in commits on deploy/glm53-kelchm, each naming its patch in an Adapted-from trailer, which recipes/glm53-kelchm/recipe.json repeats. Either way the lane's engine commit must carry the kit's LICENSE, NOTICE.md and CREDITS.md at packaging/kits/glm-5.3-flash-dgx-sparks-1104/, and the lane's image copies them to /opt/tensorfold/LICENSES/kits/. tools/check_recipe.py enforces this, except for a project the recipe lists in notices_pending: images built from such a recipe lack that project's notices, and it cannot be released.

Images built from this repository contain TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold, Apache-2.0, with earlier code under MIT) and the third-party components each Dockerfile lists. Their licence files are copied into each image under /opt/tensorfold/LICENSES.
